  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="container--narrow">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</span>
        <h2 class="section-title" id="faq-title">FAQ &mdash; vehicle wraps Rotterdam</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="faq" role="list">
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-1">What does a vehicle wrap cost in Rotterdam?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-1" role="region" hidden><p>Partial van lettering from &euro;175. Partial wrap from &euro;350. Full wrap on a passenger car from &euro;1,995; vans and transporters from &euro;2,495. Fleet programmes (5+ vehicles) from &euro;1,995 per vehicle. All prices include 21% Dutch VAT, design, A-brand cast vinyl, laminate and workshop installation.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-2">How long does a vehicle wrap last?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-2" role="region" hidden><p>Five to seven years for a properly installed wrap using 3M IJ or Avery MPI cast vinyl with laminate, parked outdoors in the Dutch climate. Indoor-parked vehicles often hold colour for ten years or more. Our warranty is two years on colour stability, adhesion and material defects.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-3">Can a wrap be removed without damaging the paint?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-3" role="region" hidden><p>Yes, when the original paintwork is intact and the wrap was installed correctly. 3M and Avery cast vinyl is designed for clean removal within seven years. After removal we polish the panels; in many cases the underlying paint looks better than before because the vinyl protected it from UV, stone chips and tar.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-4">Do you also wrap leased vehicles?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-4" role="region" hidden><p>Yes. A wrap is fully reversible: the leasing company receives the vehicle back in original paint at end of contract. We recommend partial wraps for short lease terms to limit production cost, and full wraps for terms of three years or more.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-5">What is the difference between cast vinyl and calendered vinyl?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-5" role="region" hidden><p>Cast vinyl (3M IJ, Avery MPI) is poured and cured: thin, dimensionally stable, conforms to curves and rivets, lasts five to seven years outdoors. Calendered vinyl is rolled: thicker, less conformable, suitable for flat panels, lasts three to five years. We use cast vinyl for all full and partial wraps; calendered is appropriate for flat-panel lettering only.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-6">Do you offer fleet wrap programmes?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-6" role="region" hidden><p>Yes. For fleets of five vehicles or more we run a programme with a master design, brand-consistent production and scheduled installation. For fleets of ten or more we offer an annual maintenance visit to repair stone chips or small damage.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-7">How long does the installation take?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-7" role="region" hidden><p>Partial lettering: two to four hours. Partial wrap: half to one full day. Full wrap on a car: one to two working days. Full wrap on a van or transporter: two to three working days. Workshop in Rotterdam Zuidoost; drop off and pick up complete.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq__item" role="listitem">
          <button class="faq__question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-vw-8">Which sectors use vehicle wraps most in Rotterdam?<span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
          <div class="faq__answer" id="faq-vw-8" role="region" hidden><p>Heating and cooling contractors, electrical contractors, cleaning services, food delivery, taxi and limousine, courier and last-mile logistics, port-related services, plumbers, landscapers, construction firms and fitness franchises. Essentially any trade or service business where the van is seen at the customer doorstep every day.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

